course: dictionary
lesson: 3505
title: Fast: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fast is a word with several meanings, and the words around it show you which one is meant. Its most common meaning is quick, moving or doing something at speed. «A moving swing is heavy and fast at a child's head height and can knock you out or break teeth, so walk wide around swings.» Here fast means moving very quickly.
explain: Fast can also describe a clock. A clock that is fast shows a time later than the real time. Fast can mean firmly too: «stuck fast» means stuck tightly, and «fast asleep» means very deeply asleep. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does it still make sense?
explain: Fast can be a verb as well. To fast means to go without food for a time, often for religious reasons, and a fast is that time. Science uses fast for speed: «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster, so cars and railings by the sea rust quickly.» Faster compares how quickly something happens.
fact: Fast means moving or doing something quickly.
fact: A clock or watch that is fast shows a time later than the real time.
fact: «Stuck fast» means firmly stuck; «fast asleep» means very deeply asleep.
fact: To fast means to not eat for a time; a fast is that time.
fact: Fast, faster and fastest compare speed, as in «as fast as» and «fastest time».
exercise: «A moving swing is heavy and fast at a child's head height.» What does fast mean here? | *Moving very quickly | Firmly stuck | Ahead of the real time | Not eating for a time
exercise: «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster.» Find and copy one word that compares speed. | *faster | Salt | spray | cars
exercise: A clock that is 5 minutes fast shows what? | The real time exactly | A time 5 minutes earlier than the real time | *A time later than the real time
test: «The children were fast asleep after the long walk.» What does fast mean here? | Moving at speed | *Very deeply | Not eating for a time | Very quickly
test: Ayaan says he will fast on Friday. What does fast mean? | Run around the field | *Go without food for a time | Move firmly and tightly | Eat a very big lunch
exam: «Pair the numbers from both ends to add fast: 1 + 4 = 5 and 2 + 3 = 5.» In this sentence, what does fast mean? | *Quickly | Without food for a time | A time later than the real time | Firmly
